From: Scott Iveland <scott.iveland@adtran.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 10:41:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: respect deferred probe timeout for MAC address

When MAC address retrieval returns -EPROBE_DEFER, check if the kernel's
deferred probe timeout has expired before falling back to the vendor
set_mac_addr hook or a random MAC. This allows recovery/initramfs
environments to proceed when nvmem providers are unavailable while
still waiting for deferred probes during normal boot.

Ported from the target-mediatek 990-32 patch of the same name.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -4069,9 +4069,14 @@ static int airoha_alloc_gdm_device(struc
 		return err;
 
 	err = of_get_ethdev_address(np, netdev);
-	if (err) {
+	if (err == -EPROBE_DEFER) {
+		err = driver_deferred_probe_check_state(eth->dev);
 		if (err == -EPROBE_DEFER)
 			return err;
+		dev_warn(eth->dev, "MAC address defer timeout, using fallback MAC\n");
+	}
+
+	if (err) {
 	if (eth->extra_ops.set_mac_addr)
 		eth->extra_ops.set_mac_addr(eth, netdev);
 	else {
